app.reclaim.kind_stale_deps.other = Dependencies and build output of worktrees untouched for {n} days
app.reclaim.cat_worktree = Worktree
app.reclaim.what_worktree = The folder goes to the Trash with everything in it. The branch stays (unless you tick below), so git worktree add brings it back.
app.reclaim.cat_incremental = Incremental cache (cargo)
app.reclaim.what_incremental = The next cargo build recreates it; that build is slower.
app.reclaim.cat_target = Build folder (cargo / Maven target)
app.reclaim.what_target = The next build compiles everything again from scratch.
app.reclaim.cat_node_modules = Installed packages (node_modules)
app.reclaim.what_node_modules = Run npm install (or pnpm, yarn, bun install) to get it back.
app.reclaim.cat_next = Next.js build and cache (.next)
app.reclaim.what_next = Next.js recreates it on the next dev or build run.
app.reclaim.cat_build = Build output (dist / build)
app.reclaim.what_build = Your build recreates it (npm run build, gradle build…). Only taken if git ignores everything in it.
app.reclaim.cat_gradle = Gradle project cache (.gradle)
app.reclaim.what_gradle = Gradle recreates it on the next build.
app.reclaim.cat_derived = Xcode DerivedData
app.reclaim.what_derived = Xcode rebuilds it and indexes the project again.
app.reclaim.keepers_loading = Looking for files git doesn’t track here…
app.reclaim.keepers_unknown = git couldn’t list the files it doesn’t track here; this worktree will be left alone.
app.reclaim.keepers_none = No files outside git besides build output.
